      "notes": "Pro Wrestling Tycoon is a text-heavy management simulation of the pro wrestling industry. It does not focus on graphic depictions of sexual acts. Mature themes appear mainly through simulated workplace drama, booking decisions, news, messages, and moddable content.\r\n\r\nViolence is central to the setting. Matches, angles, and show presentation can include staged combat, dangerous spots, injuries, rehab, and suspensions. Talent may suffer serious injuries, and characters can die during a save through natural causes, health issues, accidents, in-ring incidents, or overdose. These events are generally presented through text, stats, and management outcomes rather than cinematic gore, but descriptions can still be unsettling.\r\n\r\nThe game can also involve substance-related themes, including drug testing, failed tests, disciplinary consequences, rehab, and overdose-related deaths. Character relationships may include dating, marriage, breakups, and backstage conflict. Promotions can book more risqu\u00e9 creative product, and characters have adult attributes such as sexuality, but the core game is not built around explicit sexual content or depictions of sexual assault or non-consensual sex. Self-harm is not a featured theme of the base simulation.\r\n\r\nBecause the game supports custom mods and Steam Workshop content, user-created text, images, and scenarios may include stronger language or more sensitive topics than the base game. Players who want to avoid specific themes should review mods carefully before installing them."
