      "notes": "NIGHTWIRE is set in a fictional cyber-underworld and is built around stylized cybercrime: you build a data-theft operation, launder stolen data on an illegal black market, and evade law enforcement. This criminal activity is core to the game's fantasy and is presented in an abstract, systems-driven way \u2014 through nodes, meters, and markets \u2014 rather than through graphic depictions.\r\n\r\nViolence is abstract and non-graphic. Confrontations play out through on-screen integrity meters, data intrusions, and timing- and logic-based minigames. There is no blood, gore, or depiction of physical injury.\r\n\r\nThe story carries a dark, tense, psychological tone. Its central arc involves confronting a hostile \"ghost\" of a discarded version of yourself, and it explores themes of identity, memory, loss, and self-erasure \u2014 including story choices and endings about deleting, merging with, or letting go of that other self. Some players may find these existential, identity-related themes intense.\r\n\r\nNIGHTWIRE does not contain sexual content or nudity, sexual assault or non-consensual content, or depictions of self-harm, suicide, or drug or alcohol abuse."
